{
  "source": "course-assets/build-your-skills-opener/build-your-skills-opener.mp4",
  "duration": 99.776,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 2.84,
      "text": "Think back to the very first time you learned how to ride a bicycle."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.48,
      "end": 8.0,
      "text": "The actual achievement happening in your brain was developing a physical sense of balance."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.92,
      "end": 11.54,
      "text": "Fast forward a few years and you outgrew that childhood bike."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.9,
      "end": 15.12,
      "text": "You abandoned it in the garage and eventually moved on to something else."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.84,
      "end": 20.58,
      "text": "You took that ingrained sense of balance and applied it to entirely different physical environments."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.12,
      "end": 26.18,
      "text": "It is the exact same core mechanism that kept you upright the first time you tried ice skating."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.18,
      "end": 31.48,
      "text": "No one could download that coordination into your nervous system, and you couldn't buy it off a shelf."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.44,
      "end": 35.28,
      "text": "You had to earn it through the friction of your own practice."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.46,
      "end": 41.52,
      "text": "That physical dynamic maps directly onto intellectual development in the modern classroom and workplace."
    },
    {
      "start": 42.12,
      "end": 48.2,
      "text": "Thinking carefully, working alongside others, hunting for fresh ideas, and maintaining an active curiosity."
    },
    {
      "start": 48.68,
      "end": 53.62,
      "text": "You will use AI to practice, but the mental agility you build in the process goes with you everywhere."
    },
    {
      "start": 53.62,
      "end": 56.34,
      "text": "It shapes how you approach an essay in school,"
    },
    {
      "start": 56.64,
      "end": 58.42,
      "text": "how you solve a bottleneck at work,"
    },
    {
      "start": 58.42,
      "end": 60.52,
      "text": "and how you organize your daily life."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.28,
      "end": 63.78,
      "text": "When the technical tools are identical across the board,"
    },
    {
      "start": 64.06,
      "end": 66.98,
      "text": "the only variables left are your unique choices,"
    },
    {
      "start": 67.38,
      "end": 68.98,
      "text": "the specific questions you ask,"
    },
    {
      "start": 69.02,
      "end": 71.96,
      "text": "and the cultivated judgment you apply to the output."
    },
    {
      "start": 72.54,
      "end": 75.32,
      "text": "This section will help you answer three specific questions."
    },
    {
      "start": 76.02,
      "end": 78.46,
      "text": "What will set me apart in a world with AI?"
    },
    {
      "start": 79.36,
      "end": 80.38,
      "text": "Next, question two."
    },
    {
      "start": 80.76,
      "end": 82.86,
      "text": "What skills should I start building now?"
    },
    {
      "start": 82.86,
      "end": 88.84,
      "text": "Finally, question three, how can I use AI effectively and responsibly in my future work?"
    },
    {
      "start": 89.4,
      "end": 92.8,
      "text": "The tools will change. The skills are yours to keep."
    }
  ],
